  {
   "bbox": [
    41.04,
    686.52,
    276.84,
    769.68
   ],
   "id": "e14",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.76,
      686.52,
      276.48,
      695.16
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Taranna\u2019 is a new variety of the native grass Danthonia"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.4,
      697.68,
      276.12,
      706.32
     ],
     "text": "richardsonii. It is distinct from the only other known variety"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.76,
      708.48,
      276.84,
      717.48
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Hume\u2019 in having a wider inflorescence and glumes, longer"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      719.28,
      276.12,
      728.28
     ],
     "text": "flag leaves and wider flag and tiller leaves. Although the culm"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      730.44,
      276.84,
      739.44
     ],
     "text": "heights of the two varieties are similar, \u201cTaranna\u2019 has a greater"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.4,
      741.24,
      276.48,
      748.44
     ],
     "text": "internodal distance between the first and second nodes on the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      751.68,
      276.84,
      760.68
     ],
     "text": "culm. At flowering the leaves of \u2018Taranna\u2019 tend to be a darker"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      41.04,
      762.84,
      150.12,
      769.68
     ],
     "text": "colour than those of \u2018Hume\u2019."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "\u2018Taranna\u2019 is a new variety of the native grass Danthonia\nrichardsonii. It is distinct from the only other known variety\n\u2018Hume\u2019 in having a wider inflorescence and glumes, longer\nflag leaves and wider flag and tiller leaves. Although the culm\nheights of the two varieties are similar, \u201cTaranna\u2019 has a greater\ninternodal distance between the first and second nodes on the\nculm. At flowering the leaves of \u2018Taranna\u2019 tend to be a darker\ncolour than those of \u2018Hume\u2019.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    303.84,
    565.92,
    540.72,
    712.44
   ],
   "id": "e15",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.92,
      565.92,
      539.64,
      574.56
     ],
     "text": "*Taranna\u2019 is distinct from naturally occurring ecotypes in that"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      576.72,
      539.64,
      585.36
     ],
     "text": "it has a wider and longer inflorescence, a longer interbranch"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      586.08,
      539.64,
      598.32
     ],
     "text": "distance between the first and second branches of the inflores-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      598.32,
      539.64,
      606.6
     ],
     "text": "cence. \u2018Taranna\u2019 also has a longer culm and longer flag and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      609.12,
      492.84,
      617.4
     ],
     "text": "tiller leaves than the naturally occurring ecotypes."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      630.72,
      331.2,
      640.08
     ],
     "text": "Origin"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.92,
      646.92,
      540.72,
      655.92
     ],
     "text": "*Taranna\u2019 was selected by Dr G.M. Lodge from an ecotype of"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      658.08,
      540.0,
      667.08
     ],
     "text": "the native grass Danthonia richardsonii. Selection over four"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      669.24,
      539.64,
      677.88
     ],
     "text": "successive generations was based predominantly on seed reten-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      680.04,
      539.28,
      689.04
     ],
     "text": "tion and production characteristics assessed on spaced plants."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      303.84,
      689.76,
      539.64,
      701.64
     ],
     "text": "The original parent plant was collected in 1985 from a naturally"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      304.2,
      700.56,
      539.64,
      712.44
     ],
     "text": "occurring population of plants growing on a stock route on a"
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "*Taranna\u2019 is distinct from naturally occurring ecotypes in that\nit has a wider and longer inflorescence, a longer interbranch\ndistance between the first and second branches of the inflores-\ncence. \u2018Taranna\u2019 also has a longer culm and longer flag and\ntiller leaves than the naturally occurring ecotypes.\nOrigin\n*Taranna\u2019 was selected by Dr G.M. Lodge from an ecotype of\nthe native grass Danthonia richardsonii. Selection over four\nsuccessive generations was based predominantly on seed reten-\ntion and production characteristics assessed on spaced plants.\nThe original parent plant was collected in 1985 from a naturally\noccurring population of plants growing on a stock route on a",
